-- allium: 3
--
-- nixtune-page: the control flow of the nixtune page and the contracts
-- it holds with the services on the Pi. The page is a Halogen single
-- page application that speaks the MPD protocol itself over websockets
-- bridged by websocat. There is no application server and this spec
-- adds none: every capability below is reached through MPD 0.24.15, the
-- volume helper, the art cache, a static capabilities.json and the
-- browser itself.
--
-- RELATION TO nixtune.allium. That spec keeps the NixOS module, the
-- hardware, the fleet, arbitration and maintenance. Its rules and
-- surfaces about the page (ClientBrowsesFolders, ClientBrowsesTags,
-- ClientJumpsToLetter, GuestAppends, GuestCommandNotOffered,
-- HostCommands, HostReordersQueue, HostSeesAttribution, HostShowsQr,
-- ClientSetsVolume, StatusPushedToSessions, surfaces GuestPage and
-- HostPage, value BrowseColumn) are superseded by this file. Where the
-- two disagree about the page, this file holds. Where this file and the
-- code disagree, the code was read on 2026-10-31 at 1ad560b and this
-- file records the intended change.
--
-- FACTS THIS SPEC IS WRITTEN AGAINST, checked 2026-10-31:
--   - nixpkgs 6510408d builds mpd 0.24.15 with features = null, which
--     enables every known feature, pcre (pcre2), icu and sqlite
--     included. So regular expression filters, ICU collation in MPD's
--     own sorts, and the sticker database are all present.
--   - 0.24 has: addid and searchadd/findadd with a relative position
--     (+0 is "after the current song", since 0.23), sticker inc and
--     sticker dec, sticker find with sort and window, listplaylistinfo
--     with a range, the explicit case operators eq_ci, contains_ci and
--     starts_with_ci, and `added-since` filters.
--   - 0.24 does NOT have `list ... window`. That arrived in 0.25, which
--     is unreleased. nixtune.allium's claim that the unfiltered artist
--     list "is windowed" is wrong for this MPD and is dropped here.
--   - `list` collects values into a std::map<std::string> and prints
--     them in that map's order, which is BYTE order: case sensitive,
--     every upper case letter before every lower case one, and
--     anything outside ASCII after both. "dEUS" and "of Montreal" sort
--     after "Zappa". The page never shows MPD's `list` order as is.
--   - `list` and filters apply MPD's tag fallbacks
--     (src/tag/Fallback.hxx): AlbumArtist falls back to Artist;
--     AlbumArtistSort to AlbumArtist, then ArtistSort, then Artist;
--     ArtistSort to Artist; AlbumSort to Album; TitleSort to Title. A
--     song with no value at all is listed under the empty string.
--   - `find`/`search` sort accepts tag names, "Last-Modified" and
--     "Added". It does not accept duration or audio format. Without
--     `sort` the order is database order, which is directory then file
--     name, each ICU collated.
--   - max_output_buffer_size is 32768 KB (mpd.maxOutputBuffer).
--   - database.nix disables every playlist plugin, and `load` goes
--     through the same registry, so a stored playlist can be saved and
--     not loaded until m3u and extm3u are re-enabled (nixtune.allium
--     KnownIssue stored_playlists_unloadable). P12 depends on that.
--   - Halogen renders the whole page on every state update. A reply
--     collected through component state renders once per line. Since
--     1ad560b the partial tail and the reply being collected live in
--     Refs, and only a greeting or a reply's end touches state.
--   - The library: about 75.8k songs, roughly a quarter lossless. A
--     queue of 100 to 250 entries is ordinary.
--
-- Decisions taken 2026-10-31 (Harry's answers to the drill-down):
--
--   P1. SCOPE. This file covers the page, every list it draws, every
--       command it sends, and the contracts with MPD, websocat, the
--       volume helper and the art cache. It is nixtune specific: it
--       assumes this MPD, this capabilities.json, this helper and this
--       cache, and does not try to describe a generic MPD client.
--
--   P2. MPD IS THE TRUTH. The page shows what MPD last reported and
--       nothing else. A command changes nothing on screen until the idle
--       connection reports the change and the page reads it back. The
--       only page-side state that runs ahead of MPD is a DRAFT: a value
--       the person is in the middle of entering (the volume thumb, the
--       seek thumb, a typed field, a queue row being dragged). A draft
--       is visibly a draft, is dropped when MPD reports a value near
--       it, and is never sent anywhere except as the command it becomes.
--
--   P3. ONE LIST ENGINE. Every list on the page (the tag columns, the
--       track table, the queue, the folder listing, a saved playlist's
--       contents, the radio stations) is drawn by one mechanism with
--       fixed row pitch: only the rows in the viewport plus an overscan
--       are in the DOM, and spacers above and below make the scrollbar
--       the true length. What differs between lists is only how rows
--       are obtained, and that is one of three SOURCES (enum RowSource):
--         held      the whole list is in memory (a tag column, the
--                   radio list, a folder listing)
--         windowed  rows arrive in pages from a `count`-sized total
--                   (the track table, a saved playlist)
--         versioned rows arrive in windows and are kept current by
--                   MPD's playlist version (the queue)
--
--   P4. EVERY REPLY IS BOUNDED, AND THE BOUND IS WRITTEN DOWN. Each
--       command the page sends appears in table ReplyBounds with the
--       reason its reply cannot overrun the output buffer. A command
--       with no entry there is not sent. `listall`, `listallinfo` and
--       an unwindowed `find`/`search` are never sent.
--
--   P5. COLLATION IS THE PAGE'S JOB. Every tag column is ordered by the
--       page, by sort key, with the browser's locale-aware comparison
--       (Data.String.localeCompare) at base sensitivity, so case and
--       accents do not split a group. The sort key is the *Sort tag
--       where the file has one, which MPD's fallbacks supply in the same
--       reply (rule ColumnValuesArrive). Display shows the plain tag.
--       The letter rail files a row under the first letter of its SORT
--       KEY, so "The Beatles" with AlbumArtistSort "Beatles, The" sits
--       under B, and "The The" with no sort tag sits under T. Leading
--       articles are never stripped by the page itself; a library that
--       wants "Beatles" under B says so in its tags.
--
--   P6. THE CHAIN IS [GENRE] -> ALBUM ARTIST -> ALBUM. The artist column
--       is AlbumArtist, which MPD falls back to Artist for any file that
--       lacks it, so a compilation tagged "Various Artists" is one row
--       and an untagged album still appears under its track artist. The
--       genre column is off by default and is a toggle, as in the code
--       today. The selection model is the code's: plain click replaces,
--       shift extends from the anchor, ctrl/meta toggles one row; every
--       column has an All row; a change resets every column to its right
--       to All. The three selections always describe one path.
--
--   P7. OR IS A REGULAR EXPRESSION, NOT A PRODUCT OF QUERIES. MPD
--       filters have AND and NOT and no OR, so today a selection of
--       several values expands into the cartesian product of commands,
--       capped at 32 with an approximate fallback beyond. This MPD has
--       pcre, so a column selection of values v1..vn becomes ONE term:
--         (AlbumArtist =~ '^(?:v1|v2|...|vn)$')
--       with each vi escaped as a regex literal. Every column and the
--       track table are then exactly one command each, whatever is
--       selected, which also makes a global `sort` on the track table
--       possible: a sort over one query is one ordering, a sort over 32
--       queries laid end to end is 32 orderings. A selection of one
--       value uses `==` rather than a regex, because it is cheaper to
--       evaluate and reads plainly in a log. Escaping is three layers
--       and is specified in contract FilterExpression.
--
--   P8. ALBUMS IN DISCOGRAPHY ORDER. With an artist selected the album
--       column is ordered by year, then by album sort key. The year is
--       the first four digits of Date (OriginalDate is not used: it is
--       sparse in this library and MPD does not fall back from it). An
--       album with no date sorts after every dated album. With no artist
--       selected the column is the whole library's albums, ordered by
--       sort key alone, because year order across thousands of artists
--       is not a way of finding anything.
--
--   P9. SEARCH FILTERS THE COLUMNS. There is no separate result list.
--       A query adds one more term to every column's command and to the
--       track table's:
--         (any contains_ci 'q')
--       so each column shows only values that have a matching song, and
--       browsing carries on inside the result. Typing commits after a
--       pause (config search_debounce) and at two characters or more;
--       Enter commits at once; clearing the box removes the term. A
--       column narrowed by a query is never read from or written to the
--       cache. Every reply is tagged with the generation it was asked at
--       and a stale one is discarded, so fast typing never paints an
--       older result over a newer one.
--
--   P10. THE TRACK LIST IS A SORTABLE TABLE. Columns: #, Title, Artist,
--       Album, Year, Time, Format. A header click sorts by that field
--       through MPD (`find ... sort <key> window`), a second click
--       reverses (`sort -<key>`), a third returns to database order.
--       Sortable keys and what they send: # -> Track, Title ->
--       TitleSort, Artist -> ArtistSort, Album -> AlbumSort, Year ->
--       Date. Time and Format are not sortable, because MPD cannot sort
--       on them and sorting a window of 200 rows in the page would
--       disagree with the rows outside it. Their headers are not
--       buttons. The default, with no header chosen, is database order,
--       which for ripped albums is disc and track order.
--
--   P11. THE QUEUE IS WINDOWED AND VERSIONED. The queue view holds only
--       the rows near its viewport. It reads windows with
--       `playlistinfo START:END` and, when MPD's playlist version moves,
--       asks only for what changed inside the held window with
--       `plchanges <version> START:END`. The length comes from `status`
--       (playlistlength), which is how a deletion at the end is seen.
--       A whole-queue `playlistinfo` is never sent again.
--
--   P12. SAVED PLAYLISTS ARE THEIR OWN VIEW. Host only. Blocked on
--       KnownIssue stored_playlists_unloadable: until m3u and extm3u
--       are back on, Load and Append fail with an ACK and the view
--       offers Save and the listings only. Lists the saved
--       playlists (`listplaylists`), shows one's contents windowed
--       (`listplaylistinfo NAME START:END`), loads one into the queue
--       (`load`), appends one (`load` without clear), saves the queue as
--       one (`save`), renames and removes. "Add to saved playlist" on a
--       row writes with `playlistadd`.
--
--   P13. ROW ACTIONS. On the host page a track row, an album row or the
--       whole current selection offers: Add to end, Play next, Replace
--       and play, Add to saved playlist. The "whole current selection"
--       is the tracks PICKED in the table when any are (P21), and
--       otherwise everything the columns and the query narrow to. Play next is `addid <uri> +0`
--       for one track and `findadd <filter> position +0` for a
--       selection, so the songs land after the current one in their
--       table order. The guest page offers Add to end only.
--
--   P14. KEYBOARD IS TRANSPORT ONLY. Space play/pause, ArrowLeft and
--       ArrowRight previous and next, ArrowUp and ArrowDown a volume
--       step, M mute. None of them fires while focus is in a text field
--       or on a range input, which owns its own arrows. Lists are
--       pointer and touch. The queue grip's arrow keys stay, because
--       that is the non-pointer path to reordering and not navigation.
--
--   P15. THE GUEST PAGE IS SIMPLER. Search, then a stacked drill-down:
--       album artist, then album, then tracks, one choice at a time,
--       single select, with the choices made shown as chips that go
--       back. Same list engine, same commands, same cache. Guests add to
--       the end only.
--
--   P16. VETOES COUNT WITH sticker inc, NOT WITH A NAME LIST. Harry
--       picked one sticker per voter. MPD cannot count that in one
--       command: `sticker find` takes one exact sticker name, so
--       counting nixtune.veto.<nickname> stickers means one command per
--       nickname that has ever voted, and the page does not know those
--       nicknames. What removes the race without losing the one-command
--       read is `sticker inc song <uri> nixtune.vetoes 1`, which MPD
--       applies atomically. The tally is then one integer per track,
--       read for the whole queue with one `sticker find`. Which tracks
--       this browser has voted against is kept in this browser's
--       localStorage. That is the same strength as today: today's
--       one-vote-per-nickname is also enforced only by a value the
--       browser made up for itself. The voter names are no longer
--       visible to other guests; the count is.
--
--   P17. ATTRIBUTION STAYS ONE COMMAND, AND ITS GROWTH IS NAMED. `sticker
--       find song "" nixtune.added_by` returns every attribution ever
--       written. It grows with every guest add and nothing removes old
--       ones. The page reads it only while a view that shows attribution
--       is open, and open question "attribution growth" asks for a
--       measurement before a pruning rule is chosen.
--
--   P18. THE CACHE HOLDS ONLY WHOLE-LIBRARY LISTS. The three unnarrowed
--       column lists (genres, album artists, albums), with their sort
--       keys, are stored in localStorage under MPD's db_update stamp. A
--       visit whose stamp matches draws them with no request. Nothing
--       narrowed, searched or windowed is cached. A rescan moves the
--       stamp and every stored list under an older one is deleted.
--
--   P19. FFI BUDGET. Hand-written foreign modules are allowed where no
--       registry package binds what is needed, each one named in
--       contract ForeignBudget with the reason. The budget today is
--       empty: everything this spec needs is in purescript-web-html,
--       web-dom, web-uievents, web-storage and web-socket.
--
--   P20. ONE TRANSPORT BAR, PRESENT ON EVERY HOST VIEW, as decision 18
--       of nixtune.allium and as the code already does. The queue stays
--       a separate view at every width.
--
-- Recorded from the code at 1ad560b:
--
--   P21. TRACKS CAN BE PICKED. A click on a track row's body picks it:
--       plain picks that row alone, ctrl/meta adds or removes it, shift
--       takes the run from the anchor. Picks are held by URI, so they
--       survive scrolling away and the rows being refetched, and a shift
--       run covers only rows the page holds (a row it has never fetched
--       has no URI). Any change to the columns, the query or the sort
--       clears the picks, because they belonged to the list that was
--       replaced. The row's own add control still queues that one track.
--       With picks, the bulk actions name their count ("Add 3") and act
--       on the picks in TABLE order, not click order, one `add` per URI.
--       With none, they act on the whole filter. With neither picks nor
--       a filter they are not offered, because they would mean the whole
--       library.
--
--   P22. A SOCKET IS THE CANCEL. MPD cannot cancel a command it has
--       started and answers one at a time per connection. When a column
--       selection changes while the lib connection has anything asked
--       or queued, the page closes that socket and opens another; what
--       the click asks for is queued on the new socket and sent at its
--       greeting. Every socket carries a serial and every event carries
--       the serial of the socket it came from; an event from a socket
--       that is no longer its connection's is ignored, so a socket
--       closed on purpose is never taken for the player going away. MPD
--       still finishes the abandoned command; its reply goes nowhere.
--
--   P23. REQUESTS GO OUT IN THE ORDER THEY ARE WANTED. One connection
--       answers in order, so order is priority. A full reload asks for
--       the active column first, then the other columns, then the track
--       table, which with nothing selected is the most expensive query.
--       A narrowing asks for the track table first (it is what the click
--       was about) and then the columns to the right.
--
--   P24. A WINDOW REMEMBERS WHAT IT ASKED. A track page request records
--       which query, at which offset, for how many rows. A short reply
--       corrects THAT query's count. Working the query out again from the
--       row number when the reply lands is wrong once an earlier query's
--       count has turned out to be zero, and corrected the wrong query to
--       zero before 1ad560b. With P7's single query this reduces to one
--       query, and the rule still holds for the no-pcre fallback.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Given
------------------------------------------------------------

given {
    page: Page
    mpd: MpdServer
    caps: Capabilities
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- External Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

-- MPD as the page meets it: one server, many connections, one reply
-- per command per connection, in order.
external entity MpdServer {
    version: String
    has_regex: Boolean
    db_update: Integer
    song_count: Integer
    playlist_version: Integer
    playlist_length: Integer
}

-- A browser on the LAN, holding localStorage for this origin.
external entity Browser {
    storage_available: Boolean
    nickname: String?
    my_vetoes: Set<String>
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

-- capabilities.json as nix/module/ui.nix writes it. Static per
-- generation.
value Capabilities {
    hostname: String
    profile: String
    output_kind: alsa | null_output
    card: String?
    mixer: String?
    modules: Set<String>
    library: Boolean
    stations: List<Station>
    websocket_path: String
    volume_path: String?
    art_path: String?
    max_volume: Integer
    public_url: String
    host_path: String
    party: Boolean
    vetoes: Integer
}

value Station {
    name: String
    url: String
}

-- One distinct value in a tag column: what is drawn, and what it is
-- ordered and filed under.
value TagValue {
    display: String
    sort_key: String
    year: Integer?
}

value Song {
    uri: String
    title: String?
    artist: String?
    album_artist: String?
    album: String?
    date: String?
    track: String?
    disc: String?
    duration: Duration?
    position: Integer?
    id: Integer?
    name: String?
}

-- What a file is, from its extension. Unchanged from the code.
value Format {
    label: String
    quality: lossless | lossy
}

-- The part of a scrolling list on screen.
value Viewport {
    top: Number
    height: Number
}

-- The rows a list puts in the DOM.
value Slice {
    first: Integer
    count: Integer
}

-- A contiguous run of rows held for a windowed or versioned list.
value HeldRun {
    from: Integer
    rows: List<Song>
}

-- One term of a filter expression, already escaped for the filter
-- layer (contract FilterExpression), not yet quoted for the protocol.
value FilterTerm {
    text: String
}

value TrackSort {
    key: track | title_sort | artist_sort | album_sort | date
    descending: Boolean
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

contract MpdBridge {
    connect: (path: String) -> Socket
    send: (socket: Socket, line: String) -> Unit
    receive: (socket: Socket) -> Chunk

    @invariant LineFramingIsThePagesJob
        -- websocat -t frames by TCP read. A message may hold several
        -- replies or stop mid-line. Each connection keeps the unfinished
        -- tail of the last message and splits on newline; a trailing
        -- carriage return is dropped.

    @invariant LoopbackOnly
        -- websocat and MPD listen on loopback; nginx proxies /ws. 6600
        -- on the LAN is mpd.exposeOnLan's business and not the page's.

    @invariant NoRoleEnforcement
        -- The bridge cannot tell the host page from the guest page.
        -- Everything this spec says a guest cannot do is what the guest
        -- page does not offer, not what MPD refuses.

    @guidance
        -- websocat -t -E ws-l:127.0.0.1:8600 tcp:127.0.0.1:6600 as
        -- nixtune-websocket.service.
}

contract VolumeWriter {
    set: (level: Integer) -> Unit

    @invariant NeverSetvolOnAHelperHost
        -- When caps.volume_path is non-null the page never sends setvol.
        -- With the helper unreachable it says so and writes nothing.

    @invariant SameScaleAsMpd
        -- amixer -M, ALSA's normalized mapping, which is what MPD's
        -- `status` reports as volume.

    @invariant Glides
        -- A target is approached in steps of volume_glide_step every
        -- volume_glide_interval; the last value is always sent.

    @guidance
        -- One line per request, "set N", over the /volume websocket.
}

contract ArtCache {
    cover: (album_directory: String) -> Image?

    @invariant OneNamePerAlbum
        -- <art_path>/<directory of the song's URI>/cover.jpg, with %, #
        -- and ? escaped. One 404 at worst, and then the page stops.

    @invariant OnlyForFiles
        -- A stream URI (contains "://") has no cover request.
}

-- The three layers between a tag value and the wire. Getting any layer
-- wrong either matches nothing or matches the wrong thing, silently.
contract FilterExpression {
    literal: (value: String) -> String
    regex_literal: (value: String) -> String
    term_eq: (tag: String, value: String) -> FilterTerm
    term_any_of: (tag: String, values: List<String>) -> FilterTerm
    term_search: (query: String) -> FilterTerm
    conjoin: (terms: List<FilterTerm>) -> String
    protocol_quote: (expression: String) -> String

    @invariant RegexLayer
        -- regex_literal escapes every PCRE metacharacter
        -- \ ^ $ . | ? * + ( ) [ ] { } with a backslash. Applied only to
        -- values that go inside =~.

    @invariant FilterStringLayer
        -- literal and the outer step of term_* wrap a value in single
        -- quotes, escaping backslash and single quote with a backslash.
        -- This is the escaping MPD's filter parser undoes.

    @invariant ProtocolLayer
        -- protocol_quote wraps the whole expression in double quotes,
        -- escaping backslash and double quote with a backslash. This is
        -- Mpd.quote today and is what MPD's command tokenizer undoes.

    @invariant Shapes
        -- term_eq(t, v)         = (t == 'v')
        -- term_any_of(t, [v])   = term_eq(t, v)
        -- term_any_of(t, vs)    = (t =~ '^(?:r1|r2|...)$'),
        --                         ri = regex_literal(vi)
        -- term_search(q)        = (any contains_ci 'q')
        -- conjoin([])           = no filter
        -- conjoin([a])          = a
        -- conjoin([a, b, ...])  = (a AND b AND ...)
        -- A command then reads, for example:
        --   list albumartist "((genre == 'Jazz') AND (any contains_ci 'blue'))" group albumartistsort

    @invariant EmptyValueIsAValue
        -- MPD lists songs lacking a tag under "". A column never shows
        -- that row (it is not selectable), so it never reaches a filter.
        -- term_eq(t, "") would mean "has no t at all", which no control
        -- on the page asks for.
}

-- Every command the page sends and why its reply is bounded. A command
-- not listed is not sent (invariant EveryCommandIsBounded).
contract ReplyBounds {
    @invariant Table
        -- status, currentsong, stats, idle    fixed size
        -- playlistinfo START:END              <= queue_window rows
        -- plchanges V START:END               <= queue_window rows
        -- find F [sort K] window A:B          <= track_page rows
        -- count F                             one line
        -- list T F group G                    bounded by F, see below
        -- list genre group <none>             whole library, about a
        --                                     few hundred values
        -- list albumartist group albumartistsort
        --                                     whole library, about ten
        --                                     thousand pairs; cached
        -- list album group albumsort          whole library; cached
        -- lsinfo P                            one directory; the
        --                                     largest directory in
        --                                     this library is the
        --                                     bound; see open question
        -- listplaylists                       number of saved playlists
        -- playlistlength N                    two lines
        -- listplaylistinfo N A:B              <= track_page rows
        -- sticker find song "" nixtune.vetoes sorted, windowed to
        --                                     sticker_window
        -- sticker find song "" nixtune.added_by
        --                                     unbounded in principle;
        --                                     P17 and open question
        -- add, addid, findadd, delete, deleteid, move, clear, play,
        -- pause, previous, next, seekcur, random, repeat, single,
        -- consume, crossfade, load, save, rm, rename, playlistadd,
        -- sticker set, sticker inc, sticker delete, update, setvol
        -- (only with no helper)                acknowledgement only
        --
        -- A whole-library `list` has no window in MPD 0.24. The three
        -- that are sent are bounded by the library's distinct values,
        -- fit in 32768 KB with a wide margin at this library's size, and
        -- are sent at most once per db_update because of the cache.
}

-- Native code the page carries. Empty today.
contract ForeignBudget {
    @invariant Named
        -- Each foreign module is listed here with the binding it
        -- supplies and why no registry package does.

    @guidance
        -- Candidates if measurement ever calls for them, none adopted:
        -- a passive scroll listener (registry bindings register
        -- non-passive ones), and IndexedDB if the album list outgrows
        -- localStorage's quota.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

enum Role { host | guest }

enum View { now_playing | queue | library | playlists | radio | qr }

enum LibraryMode { tags | folders }

enum Conn {
    cmd     -- transport, queue, status, stickers, playlists
    | idle  -- parked in idle; reports what changed
    | lib   -- columns, track table, folders; never behind a queue read
}

enum Axis { genre | album_artist | album }

enum RowSource { held | windowed | versioned }

enum PlayState { playing | paused | stopped }

enum RowAction { add_end | play_next | replace_play | add_to_playlist }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

entity Page {
    role: Role
    view: View
    mode: LibraryMode
    caps: Capabilities
    browser: Browser
    links: Link with page = this
    status: PlayerStatus
    current: Song?
    query: String?
    query_gen: Integer
    error: String?

    library: TagBrowser with page = this
    queue: QueueList with page = this
    folders: FolderList with page = this
    playlists: PlaylistView with page = this
    drafts: Draft with page = this

    invariant OneLinkPerConn {
        for c in Conn: links.count(l => l.conn = c) <= 1
    }
}

value PlayerStatus {
    state: PlayState
    volume: Integer?
    elapsed: Number
    duration: Number
    song: Integer?
    playlist_version: Integer
    playlist_length: Integer
    random: Boolean
    repeat: Boolean
    single: Boolean
    consume: Boolean
    crossfade: Integer
    updating: Boolean
    audio: String?
    error: String?
}

-- One connection to MPD.
entity Link {
    page: Page
    conn: Conn
    serial: Integer
    ready: Boolean
    partial: Ref<String>
    block: Ref<String>
    asked: List<Request>
    queued: List<Request>

    invariant BuffersAreNotState {
        -- P2 and the lesson in FACTS: partial and block are written
        -- through Effect, never through the component's state, so a
        -- reply of any length causes exactly one render.
        true
    }

    invariant RepliesInOrder {
        -- The first reply to arrive answers asked.first. Nothing else
        -- is assumed about a reply's identity.
        true
    }

    invariant NothingSentBeforeGreeting {
        not ready implies asked.count = 0
    }
}

-- What a reply is for, with the generation it was asked at where a
-- later request can make it stale.
entity Request {
    link: Link
    kind: status | current | stats | column | track_count | track_page
          | queue_window | queue_changes | folder | stickers_added
          | stickers_vetoes | playlist_list | playlist_window
          | playlist_length
          | regex_probe | fire
    axis: Axis?
    gen: Integer?
    from: Integer?
}

-- An input in progress (P2).
entity Draft {
    page: Page
    kind: volume | seek | volume_text | row_drag
    value: String
}

-- One tag column (P5, P6, P8).
entity Column {
    browser: TagBrowser
    axis: Axis
    shown: Boolean
    values: List<TagValue>
    selected: Set<String>
    anchor: String?
    gen: Integer
    pending: Boolean
    vp: Viewport
    source: RowSource = held

    rail: values.count > config.letter_rail_threshold

    invariant SelectionIsHeld {
        selected.all(s => values.any(v => v.display = s))
    }

    invariant Ordered {
        -- By (year, sort_key) for the album column with an album
        -- artist selected; by sort_key otherwise. Comparison is
        -- localeCompare at base sensitivity. Ties by display.
        IsOrdered(values)
    }
}

entity TagBrowser {
    page: Page
    genre_column: Boolean
    columns: Column with browser = this
    tracks: TrackTable with browser = this

    shown_axes: columns where shown = true

    invariant ArtistAndAlbumAlwaysShown {
        columns.all(c => c.axis = genre or c.shown)
    }

    invariant GenreShownIffToggled {
        columns.all(c => c.axis != genre or c.shown = genre_column)
    }
}

-- The list under the columns (P10).
entity TrackTable {
    browser: TagBrowser
    total: Integer
    held: HeldRun
    pending: Boolean
    gen: Integer
    sort: TrackSort?
    vp: Viewport
    picked: Set<String>
    anchor: Integer?
    source: RowSource = windowed
}

-- The queue view (P11).
entity QueueList {
    page: Page
    version: Integer
    length: Integer
    held: HeldRun
    pending: Boolean
    vp: Viewport
    attribution: Map<String, String>
    veto_counts: Map<String, Integer>
    source: RowSource = versioned
}

entity FolderList {
    page: Page
    path: String
    entries: List<FolderEntry>
    gen: Integer
    vp: Viewport
    source: RowSource = held
}

value FolderEntry {
    kind: directory | file | playlist
    uri: String
    song: Song?
}

entity PlaylistView {
    page: Page
    names: List<String>
    open: String?
    total: Integer
    held: HeldRun
    gen: Integer
    vp: Viewport
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    row_height: Number = 40.0           -- tag columns, folder rows
    track_row_height: Number = 40.0     -- the table is one line a row
    queue_row_height: Number = 58.0     -- two lines: title, then line
    overscan: Integer = 8
    track_page: Integer = 200
    queue_window: Integer = 100
    sticker_window: Integer = 2000
    letter_rail_threshold: Integer = 40
    search_min_chars: Integer = 2
    search_debounce: Duration = 250.milliseconds
    fetch_ahead_screens: Number = 1.0
    reconnect_after: Duration = 2.seconds
    scan_poll_every: Duration = 10.seconds
    volume_floor: Integer = 1
    volume_step: Integer = 5
    unmute_floor: Integer = 20
    volume_glide_step: Integer = 4
    volume_glide_interval: Duration = 40.milliseconds
    phone_breakpoint: String = "40rem"
    bar_extras_breakpoint: String = "30rem"
    cache_version: String = "v2"
    idle_subsystems: String = "player mixer playlist options database update sticker stored_playlist"
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Start and connections --------------------------------------------------

rule PageStarts {
    when: PageLoaded(path)
    ensures:
        page.caps = FetchCapabilities()
        page.role = if path = caps.host_path then host else guest
        if page.browser.nickname = null:
            page.browser.nickname = GeneratedNickname()
        LinkOpened(conn: cmd)
        LinkOpened(conn: idle)
        LinkOpened(conn: lib)
        if caps.volume_path != null:
            VolumeLinkOpened()

    @guidance
        -- capabilities.json failing to load is the one error with no
        -- recovery short of a reload, and is shown as such.
}

rule LinkGreeted {
    when: LineReceived(link, line)
    requires: IsGreeting(line)
    ensures:
        link.ready = true
        mpd.version = VersionOf(line)
        for r in link.queued:
            Sent(link, r)
        link.queued = []
        if link.conn = cmd:
            Sent(link, Request{kind: status})
            Sent(link, Request{kind: current})
            Sent(link, Request{kind: stats})
            Sent(link, Request{kind: regex_probe})
        if link.conn = idle:
            Sent(link, "idle " + config.idle_subsystems)
        if link.conn = lib and page.view = library:
            LibraryReloaded()

    @guidance
        -- A request made before its link has greeted is queued on that
        -- link, not dropped. The three sockets greet in any order.
}

rule RegexProbed {
    when: ReplyArrived(request, ok)
    requires: request.kind = regex_probe
    ensures: mpd.has_regex = ok

    @guidance
        -- `find "(title =~ '^$')" window 0:1`. An ACK means MPD was
        -- built without pcre. On this host it never ACKs (FACTS). If it
        -- did, the page shows an error naming the missing feature and
        -- the tag browser offers single selection only, rather than
        -- silently falling back to the cartesian product.
}

rule LinkLost {
    when: SocketClosed(link, serial)
    requires: serial = link.serial
    ensures:
        for r in link.asked:
            RequestAbandoned(r)
        link.ready = false
        page.error = "The player went away. Reconnecting."
        after config.reconnect_after: LinkOpened(conn: link.conn)

    @guidance
        -- An abandoned request clears the pending flag of whatever was
        -- waiting for it, so nothing waits forever for a reply that went
        -- down with the socket. The greeting on the new socket asks
        -- again for what the open view needs.
}

rule LibraryCancelled {
    when: ColumnsNarrowed(from)
    let k = page.links.find(l => l.conn = lib)
    requires: k.asked.count > 0 or k.queued.count > 0
    ensures:
        for c in library.columns: c.pending = false
        library.tracks.pending = false
        SocketClosedOnPurpose(k)
        LinkOpened(conn: lib, serial: k.serial + 1)

    @guidance
        -- P22. Runs before the narrowing sends anything, so every request
        -- the narrowing makes is queued on the new socket.
}

rule ReplyRead {
    when: LineReceived(link, line)
    requires: IsEnd(line)
    let r = link.asked.first
    ensures:
        link.asked = link.asked.rest
        if IsError(line) and r.kind not in {stickers_added, stickers_vetoes, regex_probe}:
            page.error = line
        if not IsError(line):
            ReplyArrived(request: r, ok: true, lines: link.lines)
        link.lines = []
}

-- What changed -----------------------------------------------------------

rule IdleReports {
    when: IdleChanged(subsystems)
    ensures:
        Sent(cmd, Request{kind: status})
        if "player" in subsystems:
            Sent(cmd, Request{kind: current})
        if "playlist" in subsystems and page.view = queue:
            QueueChangesRequested()
        if "sticker" in subsystems and page.view = queue:
            StickersRequested()
        if "database" in subsystems or "update" in subsystems:
            Sent(cmd, Request{kind: stats})
        if "stored_playlist" in subsystems and page.view = playlists:
            Sent(cmd, Request{kind: playlist_list})
        Sent(idle, "idle " + config.idle_subsystems)

    @guidance
        -- currentsong only on "player": today it goes out on every idle
        -- event, which on a busy queue is one wasted round trip per
        -- change. The volume comes back in `status` on "mixer".
}

rule StatsArrive {
    when: ReplyArrived(request, lines)
    requires: request.kind = stats
    let stamp = DbUpdateOf(lines)
    ensures:
        mpd.song_count = SongsOf(lines)
        if stamp != mpd.db_update:
            mpd.db_update = stamp
            CachePruned(keep: stamp)
            if page.view = library:
                LibraryReloaded()
}

rule ScanIsWatched {
    when: Tick()
    requires: page.status.updating
    ensures:
        every config.scan_poll_every:
            Sent(cmd, Request{kind: stats})
            if page.view = library:
                ColumnsRecounted()

    @guidance
        -- A scan that runs for days moves db_update only at its end, so
        -- the counts are refreshed on a timer while `updating_db` is in
        -- `status`, bypassing the cache, without moving any selection
        -- or scroll position.
}

-- The tag browser ----------------------------------------------------------

rule ColumnRequested {
    when: ColumnLoad(column)
    let filter = ColumnFilter(column)
    ensures:
        if filter = none and page.query = null and CacheHas(column.axis, mpd.db_update):
            ColumnValuesArrive(column: column, values: CacheRead(column.axis, mpd.db_update), from_cache: true)
        else:
            column.gen = column.gen + 1
            column.pending = true
            Sent(lib, Request{kind: column, axis: column.axis, gen: column.gen}, ListCommand(column, filter))

    @guidance
        -- ColumnFilter(c) conjoins term_any_of over every shown column to
        -- the left of c that has a selection, plus term_search(query)
        -- when a query is committed. ListCommand by axis:
        --   genre         list genre <F>
        --   album_artist  list albumartist <F> group albumartistsort
        --   album, with an album artist selected
        --                 list album <F> group date group albumsort
        --   album, otherwise
        --                 list album <F> group albumsort
        -- One command per column, whatever is selected (P7). The column
        -- keeps showing its previous values until the reply is complete.
}

rule ColumnValuesArrive {
    when: ReplyArrived(request, lines)
    requires: request.kind = column
    let column = request.axis.column
    requires: request.gen = column.gen
    let values = Collate(column, ParseGrouped(lines))
    ensures:
        column.pending = false
        column.values = values
        column.selected = column.selected where values.any(v => v.display = s)
        if column.anchor not in values.display:
            column.anchor = null
        if values != previous(column.values):
            ScrollKept(column)
        if column.selected != previous(column.selected):
            ColumnsNarrowed(from: column)
        if ColumnFilter(column) = none and page.query = null:
            CacheWritten(column.axis, mpd.db_update, values)

    @guidance
        -- ParseGrouped reads `list ... group` output, which MPD prints
        -- outer group first: a "AlbumArtistSort: k" line sets the
        -- current key and the "AlbumArtist: v" lines after it carry that
        -- key; likewise "Date:" then "AlbumSort:" then "Album:". Values
        -- equal to "" are dropped. A display value that appears under
        -- several keys (files tagged inconsistently) is kept once, under
        -- its lowest key. The year is the first four characters of Date
        -- when they are digits, else none.
        -- ScrollKept: when the list changed, the first selected row goes
        -- to the top; with no selection the value that was at the top
        -- stays at the top; when the list did not change nothing moves.
        -- A reply whose gen is not the column's current gen is
        -- discarded.
}

rule ValueChosen {
    when: Choose(column, value, modifier)
    requires: column.shown
    ensures:
        column.selected =
            if modifier = shift: SpanBetween(column.anchor or value, value, column.values)
            else if modifier = toggle: Toggled(value, column.selected)
            else: {value}
        column.anchor = if modifier = shift: column.anchor or value else: value
        if column.selected != previous(column.selected):
            ColumnsNarrowed(from: column)

    @guidance
        -- The clicked column is not reloaded and not scrolled. On the
        -- guest page modifier is always plain (P15).
}

rule ColumnCleared {
    when: ClearColumn(column)
    requires: column.selected.count > 0
    ensures:
        column.selected = {}
        column.anchor = null
        ColumnsNarrowed(from: column)
}

rule ColumnsNarrowed {
    when: ColumnsNarrowed(from)
    ensures:
        for c in RightOf(from):
            c.selected = {}
            c.anchor = null
            c.values = []
            c.vp.top = 0
        TrackTableReset()
        for c in RightOf(from):
            ColumnLoad(column: c)

    @guidance
        -- Every column to the right is cleared before any of them is
        -- asked for, because each one's filter depends on every column
        -- to its left. The track table goes first (P23).
}

rule GenreToggled {
    when: ToggleGenreColumn()
    ensures:
        library.genre_column = not library.genre_column
        for c in library.columns:
            c.selected = {}
            c.anchor = null
        LibraryReloaded()
}

rule LetterJumped {
    when: JumpTo(column, letter)
    requires: column.rail
    ensures: ColumnScrolledTo(column, FirstRowUnder(letter, column.values))

    @guidance
        -- Filing is by the first character of sort_key, upper-cased,
        -- with A to Z its own letter and everything else under #.
        -- Letters with no rows are drawn disabled. Because the column is
        -- ordered by the same key the rail files by, each letter's rows
        -- are contiguous, which byte-ordered MPD output did not
        -- guarantee.
}

rule SearchTyped {
    when: QueryEdited(text)
    ensures:
        page.query_draft = text
        after config.search_debounce without another QueryEdited:
            QueryCommitted(text)
}

rule SearchCommitted {
    when: QueryCommitted(text)
    let q = if Length(Trim(text)) >= config.search_min_chars: Trim(text) else: null
    requires: q != page.query
    ensures:
        page.query = q
        page.query_gen = page.query_gen + 1
        LibraryReloaded()

    @guidance
        -- Enter commits at once, below the minimum as well, so a
        -- one-letter query is possible on purpose. Selections are kept
        -- across a query change; a selection the narrowed column no
        -- longer holds is dropped by ColumnValuesArrive like any other.
        -- The guest page applies the same term to its drill-down.
}

rule LibraryReloaded {
    when: LibraryReloaded()
    let first = ActiveColumn(library)
    ensures:
        ColumnLoad(column: first)
        for c in library.shown_axes where c != first:
            ColumnLoad(column: c)
        TrackTableReset()

    @guidance
        -- P23. ActiveColumn is the first shown column with nothing
        -- selected, else the last.
}

-- The track table ----------------------------------------------------------

rule TrackTableReset {
    when: TrackTableReset()
    let t = library.tracks
    let f = TrackFilter()
    ensures:
        t.gen = t.gen + 1
        t.picked = {}
        t.anchor = null
        t.held = { from: 0, rows: [] }
        t.vp.top = 0
        t.total = if f = none: mpd.song_count else: 0
        if f != none:
            Sent(lib, Request{kind: track_count, gen: t.gen}, "count " + f)
        TrackPageRequested(from: 0)

    @guidance
        -- TrackFilter conjoins term_any_of over every shown column with a
        -- selection, plus the search term. The first page goes out
        -- beside the count, not behind it: row zero exists whatever the
        -- count turns out to be.
}

rule TrackPageRequested {
    when: TrackPageRequested(from)
    let t = library.tracks
    requires: not t.pending
    ensures:
        t.pending = true
        Sent(lib, Request{kind: track_page, gen: t.gen, from: from},
             TrackCommand(TrackFilter(), t.sort, from, from + config.track_page))

    @guidance
        -- TrackCommand:
        --   no filter, no sort   search any "" window A:B
        --   otherwise            find <F> [sort [-]<key>] window A:B
        -- `search any ""` is the one filter MPD accepts for "every
        -- song", and with no sort it is database order.
}

rule TrackPageArrives {
    when: ReplyArrived(request, lines)
    requires: request.kind = track_page
    let t = library.tracks
    requires: request.gen = t.gen
    let rows = ParseSongs(lines)
    ensures:
        t.pending = false
        if request.from = t.held.from + t.held.rows.count:
            t.held.rows = t.held.rows + rows
        if rows.count < config.track_page:
            t.total = request.from + rows.count
        else if t.total < request.from + rows.count:
            t.total = request.from + rows.count
        TrackFetchChecked()

    @guidance
        -- A short page says where the result really ends; `find` is the
        -- truth and `count` was the estimate.
}

rule TrackCountArrives {
    when: ReplyArrived(request, lines)
    requires: request.kind = track_count
    requires: request.gen = library.tracks.gen
    ensures:
        library.tracks.total = CountOf(lines)
        TrackFetchChecked()
}

rule TrackFetchChecked {
    when: TrackFetchChecked() or TrackScrolled()
    let t = library.tracks
    let want = TopRow(t.vp, config.track_row_height)
    let held_to = t.held.from + t.held.rows.count
    let reach = Ceil((t.vp.top + t.vp.height * (1 + config.fetch_ahead_screens)) / config.track_row_height)
    requires: not t.pending and t.total > 0
    ensures:
        if want < t.held.from or want >= held_to:
            t.held = { from: Floor(want / config.track_page) * config.track_page, rows: [] }
            TrackPageRequested(from: t.held.from)
        else if reach >= held_to and held_to < t.total:
            TrackPageRequested(from: held_to)

    @guidance
        -- A dragged scrollbar lands outside the held run; the run starts
        -- over on a page boundary under the viewport rather than walking
        -- there one page at a time.
}

rule TrackSorted {
    when: HeaderClicked(key)
    requires: key in {track, title_sort, artist_sort, album_sort, date}
    let s = library.tracks.sort
    ensures:
        library.tracks.sort =
            if s = null or s.key != key: { key: key, descending: false }
            else if not s.descending: { key: key, descending: true }
            else: null
        TrackTableReset()
}

rule TrackPicked {
    when: PickTrack(row, modifier)
    let t = library.tracks
    let s = t.held.rows[row - t.held.from]
    requires: s != null
    ensures:
        t.picked =
            if modifier = shift: UrisOfHeldRows(t.anchor or row, row)
            else if modifier = toggle: Toggled(s.uri, t.picked)
            else: {s.uri}
        t.anchor = if modifier = shift: t.anchor or row else: row

    @guidance
        -- P21. On the guest page there is no picking (P15).
}

rule PicksCleared {
    when: ClearPicks()
    ensures:
        library.tracks.picked = {}
        library.tracks.anchor = null
}

-- The queue ------------------------------------------------------------------

rule QueueOpened {
    when: Open(queue)
    ensures:
        page.view = queue
        page.queue.held = { from: WindowStart(page.queue.vp), rows: [] }
        page.queue.version = page.status.playlist_version
        Sent(cmd, Request{kind: queue_window, from: page.queue.held.from},
             "playlistinfo " + page.queue.held.from + ":" + (page.queue.held.from + config.queue_window))
        StickersRequested()

    @guidance
        -- WindowStart centres the window on the current song the first
        -- time the view opens in a session, and on the remembered scroll
        -- position after that.
}

rule QueueChangesRequested {
    when: QueueChangesRequested()
    let q = page.queue
    let a = q.held.from
    let b = q.held.from + q.held.rows.count
    ensures:
        Sent(cmd, Request{kind: queue_changes, from: a},
             "plchanges " + q.version + " " + a + ":" + Max(b, a + config.queue_window))
}

rule QueueChangesArrive {
    when: ReplyArrived(request, lines)
    requires: request.kind = queue_changes
    let q = page.queue
    ensures:
        for s in ParseSongs(lines):
            q.held.rows[s.position - q.held.from] = s
        q.length = page.status.playlist_length
        q.held.rows = q.held.rows where position < q.length
        q.version = page.status.playlist_version

    @guidance
        -- plchanges reports every song whose position or id changed
        -- inside the range, with its new position. A move near the top
        -- of a long queue shifts every row below it, and the range keeps
        -- that reply to the held window. Rows past playlistlength have
        -- been deleted from the end. If the version jumped by more than
        -- the held window can explain (a `clear`, a `load`), the reply
        -- simply covers the whole window, which is the same as a fresh
        -- read.
}

rule QueueScrolled {
    when: QueueScrolled(vp)
    let q = page.queue
    let want = TopRow(vp, config.queue_row_height)
    ensures:
        q.vp = vp
        if want < q.held.from or want + VisibleRows(vp) > q.held.from + q.held.rows.count:
            q.held = { from: Max(0, want - config.queue_window / 4), rows: [] }
            Sent(cmd, Request{kind: queue_window, from: q.held.from},
                 "playlistinfo " + q.held.from + ":" + (q.held.from + config.queue_window))
}

rule StickersRequested {
    when: StickersRequested()
    ensures:
        if page.role = host or caps.party:
            Sent(cmd, Request{kind: stickers_added}, "sticker find song \"\" nixtune.added_by")
        if caps.party:
            Sent(cmd, Request{kind: stickers_vetoes},
                 "sticker find song \"\" nixtune.vetoes sort value_int window 0:" + config.sticker_window)
}

rule HostReorders {
    when: RowDropped(from, to)
    requires: page.role = host
    requires: from != to
    ensures: Sent(cmd, "move " + from + " " + to)

    @guidance
        -- The drag is a Draft (P2): rows measured once on grab, drawn
        -- offset, one `move` on release, the real order back through
        -- idle and plchanges. With the queue windowed, a drag is
        -- confined to the held window; dragging past its edge scrolls
        -- the list, which extends the window, and the drop target is
        -- still a position.
}

-- Row actions --------------------------------------------------------------

rule RowActed {
    when: RowAction(action, target)
    requires: page.role = host or action = add_end
    ensures:
        if action = add_end:
            Sent(cmd, AddCommand(target, position: none))
        if action = play_next:
            Sent(cmd, AddCommand(target, position: "+0"))
        if action = replace_play:
            Sent(cmd, "clear")
            Sent(cmd, AddCommand(target, position: none))
            Sent(cmd, "play")
        if action = add_to_playlist:
            PlaylistPickerOpened(target)
        if page.role = guest:
            AttributionWritten(target)
            if page.status.state = stopped:
                Sent(cmd, "play")

    @guidance
        -- AddCommand by target:
        --   one track            add <uri> | addid <uri> +0
        --   a folder             add <uri> (position not supported for
        --                        a directory; Play next on a folder
        --                        uses findadd "(base '<uri>')" position +0)
        --   picked tracks        add <uri> per pick in table order, or
        --                        addid <uri> +i for Play next, i counting
        --                        from 0, so they land after the current
        --                        song in table order
        --   a column value or the whole filter
        --                        findadd <F> [sort [-]<key>] [position +0]
        --   a station            add <url>
        -- findadd keeps the table's current sort, so what is queued is in
        -- the order the person was looking at.
        -- AttributionWritten: one `sticker set song <uri>
        -- nixtune.added_by <nick>` per TRACK URI. A guest adding an album
        -- writes one per track, which is why the guest page adds a
        -- selection only as one findadd and attributes its tracks from
        -- the rows it already holds; tracks beyond the held rows stay
        -- unattributed. A folder is unattributed, as today.
}

rule AddedToPlaylist {
    when: PlaylistPicked(target, name)
    requires: page.role = host
    ensures:
        if target is track:
            Sent(cmd, "playlistadd " + Quote(name) + " " + Quote(target.uri))
        else:
            Sent(cmd, "searchaddpl " + Quote(name) + " " + Quote(TargetFilter(target)))
}

-- Saved playlists ------------------------------------------------------------

rule PlaylistsOpened {
    when: Open(playlists)
    requires: page.role = host
    ensures:
        page.view = playlists
        Sent(cmd, Request{kind: playlist_list}, "listplaylists")
}

rule PlaylistOpened {
    when: OpenPlaylist(name)
    ensures:
        page.playlists.open = name
        page.playlists.gen = page.playlists.gen + 1
        page.playlists.held = { from: 0, rows: [] }
        Sent(cmd, Request{kind: playlist_window, gen: page.playlists.gen, from: 0},
             "listplaylistinfo " + Quote(name) + " 0:" + config.track_page)
        Sent(cmd, Request{kind: playlist_length, gen: page.playlists.gen}, "playlistlength " + Quote(name))

    @guidance
        -- The total comes from `playlistlength NAME`, sent beside the
        -- first window, so the scrollbar is the real length at once.
        -- Load, Append, Save queue as, Rename and Delete send `load`
        -- (after `clear` for Load), `load`, `save`, `rename`, `rm`.
}

-- Folders --------------------------------------------------------------------

rule FolderBrowsed {
    when: Browse(path)
    ensures:
        page.folders.gen = page.folders.gen + 1
        Sent(lib, Request{kind: folder, gen: page.folders.gen}, "lsinfo " + Quote(path))

    @guidance
        -- Held, drawn by the list engine, so a directory of thousands is
        -- thousands of entries in memory and a few dozen in the DOM.
        -- `lsinfo` has no window in any MPD version; open question
        -- "largest directory" asks for the bound.
}

-- Party mode -----------------------------------------------------------------

rule GuestVetoes {
    when: Veto(song)
    requires: caps.party
    requires: song.uri not in page.browser.my_vetoes
    ensures:
        page.browser.my_vetoes = page.browser.my_vetoes + {song.uri}
        Sent(cmd, "sticker inc song " + Quote(song.uri) + " nixtune.vetoes 1")
        Sent(cmd, Request{kind: stickers_vetoes})
}

rule VetoLimitReached {
    when: ReplyArrived(request, lines)
    requires: request.kind = stickers_vetoes
    ensures:
        page.queue.veto_counts = ParseStickers(lines)
        for (uri, n) in page.queue.veto_counts where n >= caps.vetoes and uri in page.browser.my_vetoes:
            for s in page.queue.held.rows where s.uri = uri:
                Sent(cmd, "deleteid " + s.id)
            Sent(cmd, "sticker delete song " + Quote(uri) + " nixtune.vetoes")

    @guidance
        -- Only a browser that voted on a track acts on its limit, so a
        -- page that merely watches never deletes. Two voters that both
        -- see the limit both send deleteid; the second gets an ACK for a
        -- missing id, which is harmless and not shown. Copies of the
        -- track outside the held window are not removed by this page;
        -- they carry the same tally and go when they come into someone's
        -- held window. my_vetoes keeps entries for tracks no longer
        -- queued; it is pruned to the URIs in veto_counts on each read.
}

-- Transport and volume ------------------------------------------------------

rule KeyPressed {
    when: KeyDown(key, focus)
    requires: page.role = host
    requires: focus not in {text_input, range_input, grip}
    ensures:
        if key = " ": Sent(cmd, if page.status.state = playing: "pause 1" else: "play")
        if key = "ArrowLeft": Sent(cmd, "previous")
        if key = "ArrowRight": Sent(cmd, "next")
        if key = "ArrowUp": VolumeNudged(+config.volume_step)
        if key = "ArrowDown": VolumeNudged(-config.volume_step)
        if key = "m": MuteToggled()
}

rule VolumeSet {
    when: VolumeTarget(level)
    requires: page.role = host
    requires: level >= 0 and level <= caps.max_volume
    ensures:
        Draft{kind: volume, value: level}
        if caps.volume_path != null:
            VolumeWriter.set(level)
        else:
            Sent(cmd, "setvol " + level)

    @guidance
        -- The draft is dropped when `status` reports a level within one
        -- of it. The slider's floor is volume_floor; zero belongs to
        -- mute, which remembers the level to return to (unmute_floor
        -- when none).
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant EveryCommandIsBounded {
    for c in CommandsThePageSends:
        c.verb in ReplyBounds.Table
}

invariant NoWholeQueueRead {
    not PageSends("playlistinfo") without range
}

invariant NoUnwindowedSongListing {
    for c in CommandsThePageSends where c.verb in {"find", "search", "listplaylistinfo"}:
        HasWindow(c)
}

invariant OneCommandPerColumn {
    -- P7. Selecting forty album artists sends one `list album`, not
    -- forty.
    for col in Columns:
        RequestsInFlight(col) <= 1
}

invariant StaleRepliesDiscarded {
    for r in Replies where r.request.gen != null:
        r.request.gen != CurrentGen(r.request) implies Discarded(r)
}

invariant ColumnsInPageOrder {
    -- P5. MPD's byte order never reaches the screen.
    for col in Columns: Ordered(col.values, by: SortKeyThenDisplay)
}

invariant DomIsBounded {
    -- P3. Every list puts at most its visible rows plus 2 * overscan in
    -- the DOM.
    for l in Lists:
        RowsInDom(l) <= VisibleRows(l.vp) + 2 * config.overscan
}

invariant DraftsAreTheOnlyAheadState {
    -- P2.
    for v in ShownValues:
        v.source in {mpd_reply, draft, capabilities, local_storage}
}

invariant GuestOffersAppendOnly {
    for s in Pages where role = guest:
        not Offered(s, any of {"delete", "deleteid", "clear", "move",
                               "previous", "next", "pause", "setvol",
                               "addid +0", "load", "save", "rm"})
}

invariant TransportAlwaysReachable {
    for s in Pages where role = host:
        Offered(s, "transport") and Offered(s, "volume")
}

invariant NeverSetvolOnHelperHost {
    caps.volume_path != null implies not PageSends("setvol")
}

invariant PicksBelongToTheList {
    -- P21.
    for p in library.tracks.picked:
        WasHeldInGeneration(p, library.tracks.gen)
}

invariant StaleSocketEventsIgnored {
    -- P22.
    for e in SocketEvents:
        e.serial != LinkOf(e.conn).serial implies Ignored(e)
}

invariant CacheOnlyWholeLibrary {
    for w in CacheWrites:
        w.filter = none and w.query = null
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actors
------------------------------------------------------------

actor Host {
    identified_by: Page where role = host
}

actor Guest {
    identified_by: Page where role = guest
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

surface HostPage {
    facing host: Host

    exposes:
        page.status
        page.current
        page.queue
        page.library
        page.folders
        page.playlists
        caps.stations
        caps.public_url
        caps.modules

    provides:
        Open(view)
        Choose(column, value, modifier)
        ClearColumn(column)
        PickTrack(row, modifier)
        ClearPicks()
        ToggleGenreColumn()
        JumpTo(column, letter)
        QueryEdited(text)
        QueryCommitted(text)
        HeaderClicked(key)
        RowAction(action, target)
        PlaylistPicked(target, name)
        OpenPlaylist(name)
        Browse(path)
        RowDropped(from, to)
        VolumeTarget(level)
        KeyDown(key, focus)

    contracts:
        demands MpdBridge
        demands VolumeWriter
        demands ArtCache
        demands FilterExpression
        demands ReplyBounds

    @guarantee NoSettingsSurface
        -- Hardware, modules and stations are shown, never edited.
        -- Random, repeat, single, consume and crossfade are MPD state
        -- and the page changes them.

    @guidance
        -- Views: Now playing, Queue, Library, Playlists, Radio, QR.
        -- Library, at desktop width (above phone_breakpoint):
        --   one row: search box, Tags/Folders switch, Genre toggle,
        --            Rescan
        --   one row: the shown columns side by side, each with a header
        --            (name, selection count, clear), an All row, a
        --            letter rail when over the threshold
        --   one row: the scope in words ("Miles Davis, 3 albums"), Add,
        --            Play next, Play, Add to playlist for the whole
        --            selection
        --   the rest: the track table, header row fixed, body scrolling
        -- Library, at phone width: the active column only (the first
        -- with nothing selected, else the last), choices above it as
        -- chips; the track table becomes two-line rows with Title on top
        -- and Artist, Album, Time under it, and the sort control is a
        -- select above the list rather than headers.
        -- Every row carries its actions behind one control at phone
        -- width and as visible buttons at desktop width.
        -- Below every view, the transport bar (P20).
}

surface GuestPage {
    facing guest: Guest

    exposes:
        page.status.state
        page.current
        page.library
        page.browser.nickname
        page.queue when caps.party

    provides:
        Open(view) where view in {now_playing, library, queue}
        Choose(column, value, plain)
        ClearColumn(column)
        QueryEdited(text)
        QueryCommitted(text)
        RowAction(add_end, target)
        Veto(song) when caps.party

    contracts:
        demands MpdBridge
        demands ArtCache
        demands FilterExpression
        demands ReplyBounds

    @guarantee AppendOnlyByConstruction
        -- No control sends a queue command other than add/findadd, and
        -- `play` from the stopped state only.

    @guidance
        -- Library is P15: search box, then album artist, then album,
        -- then tracks, one at a time, chips to go back. No genre, no
        -- multi-select, no sort headers, no folder tree. Queue appears
        -- only in party mode, read only, with the veto control and its
        -- count.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred MpdProtocol.filters        -- see: doc/protocol.rst, "Filters", MPD 0.24
deferred MpdProtocol.list           -- see: doc/protocol.rst, `list`, `group`
deferred MpdProtocol.queue          -- see: `playlistinfo`, `plchanges`, `addid`, `findadd ... position`
deferred MpdProtocol.stickers       -- see: `sticker inc`, `sticker find ... sort window`
deferred MpdProtocol.storedPlaylists -- see: `listplaylists`, `listplaylistinfo`, `playlistadd`, `searchaddpl`
deferred Mpd.tagFallback            -- see: src/tag/Fallback.hxx
deferred Mpd.uniqueTagOrder         -- see: src/db/UniqueTags.cxx, src/util/RecursiveMap.hxx
deferred Browser.localeCompare      -- see: Data.String.localeCompare, ECMA-402
deferred Nixtune.system             -- see: nixtune.allium

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "attribution growth: how many nixtune.added_by stickers exist after a month of parties, and how large is the `sticker find` reply. If it grows past sticker_window, the choices are a value carrying the add time with the page deleting entries older than a day when it reads them, or attribution kept only for the held queue window with one `sticker get` per visible row."
open question "largest directory: the biggest single directory under Music/, in entries, which is the real bound on an `lsinfo` reply. If it is over a few thousand, the folder view should list subdirectories with `lsinfo` and files with `find \"(base '<dir>')\" window`, which is windowable."
open question "Whether `=~` against AlbumArtist applies MPD's fallback to Artist the way `==` does. The documentation says the fallback applies to the tag in a filter without naming the operator; one query on the real database settles it, and if it does not apply, term_any_of for album_artist becomes ((AlbumArtist =~ R) OR-equivalent) which MPD cannot express, and the regex has to be over Artist for untagged files."
open question "Whether ten thousand album artists and the whole album list, with their sort keys, fit in localStorage beside everything else the origin stores. If a write throws, the page already carries on without the cache; whether that is acceptable or calls for IndexedDB (the one candidate in ForeignBudget) depends on how often it happens."
open question "Year order uses Date. If this library's Date tags are mostly full release dates of reissues, OriginalDate would order a discography better and needs its own fallback in the page, since MPD has none from OriginalDate to Date."
open question "Whether the guest's `play` from the stopped state is welcome at 2 a.m. (carried from nixtune.allium)."
